    "q-65235": {
      "dom_id": "step-q65235",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }(1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }(1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \n$$",
